\fs32 Apollo Brand Identity\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Header Paragraph:\'a0
\f2 \

\f1 A full brand identity system for Apollo, a Science-Fiction Fantasy Library of the 21st Century located in San Francisco, CA. The work covers the complete brand architecture: research and mind mapping, combination marks, color system, typography, program logos, iconography, a campaign poster series, and a speculative wayfinding system.
\f2 \
\

\f1 01 Project Overview & Concept
\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\b \cf0 Apollo's mission:
\f4\b0  to foster a community where children and adults are encouraged to dream, create, learn, and collaborate.
\f2\i0 \

\f4\i The brand needed to communicate wonder, curiosity, and the joy of discovery through a visual system sophisticated enough to function across every library touchpoint. The project was developed as part of a branding design course in the MFA Communication Design program at Pratt Institute.
\f0\i0\fs32 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf2 \
 Inspiration: Knowledge + Science + Fantasy = Apollo\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 02 Visual Language: Research & Mind Map
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 Apollo's core identity pulls in five different directions: Library, Science, Space, Fantasy, and the Greek god for which the library is named. Each branch opened into its own constellation of associations, and together they shaped the conceptual foundation before any visual decisions were made.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 03 visual language: Color System
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 Bold, optimistic, and built to hold two things at once: the serious science behind the library and the joyful energy it aims to inspire. The palette works across digital and large-format print.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 04 visual language: typography
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 A bold geometric display face for headlines. An approachable humanist sans-serif for body copy and exhibit labels. The two work together across every scale, from large wayfinding totems to small room identifiers.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 05 visual language: Icon System
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 A custom icon set covers the library's navigation and programming categories: astronomy, chemistry, biology, physics, and beyond. Every icon is drawn on a consistent grid, calibrated to read clearly at wayfinding scale.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 06 identifier: Combination Mark
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 The combination mark pairs a custom logotype with a geometric symbol inspired by orbital paths and the arc of discovery. The system includes primary, stacked, and symbol-only variants, each tested across signage and print contexts.
\f2\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 07 Identifier: Program logos\'a0
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 Program logos extend the identity into Apollo's individual departments and programming areas. Each maintains a visual connection to the core mark while developing its own distinct character.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 08 environment: Wayfinding system
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 A speculative wayfinding system shows how the brand lives in the library environment. Color-coded zones, icon-based navigation, and consistent typography carry the identity across signage at every scale.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 09 Campaign Posters
\f2\fs24 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 Four campaign posters show the brand out in the world. Each image traces back to the mind map. The god Apollo speaks to Fantasy, the moon and night sky to Science and Space, and an open book to the Library. Each poster is a different answer to the same question: what does Apollo mean?
\f2\fs24 \
\

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 10 Campaign in Context\'a0
\f2\fs24 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 Apollo's campaign posters applied across real-world environments: city streets, transit banners, and public poster frames.
\f2\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \cf0 \strokec3 11 Final outcome & reflection
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 Apollo operates across every level of a brand system: identity, iconography, print, and environmental design. Working across all those deliverables at once required systemic thinking. Every decision in one area had consequences in another. The system only worked if it held together as a whole.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \

\f1\fs29\fsmilli14667 \strokec3 This project reinforced that brand identity is not just a logo. It is a system of decisions that must hold across every surface it touches, from a poster to a building. Designing the wayfinding system pushed me to think beyond the page and consider how a brand inhabits physical space and how visitors actually move through and read an environment. Apollo demanded a visual language flexible enough to hold knowledge, science, and fantasy at once. Building that system taught me what it actually means to design one.
\f2\fs24 \strokec3 \
